#Other Information
#Environmental Parameters (and sensors to which they are applied)
#Hole Size 				: 8.5" (all sensors)
#Tool Size 				: 6.75"
#Mud Type 				: WBM (Gamma Ray)
#Mud Weight 				: 1.25 - 1.29 SG (Gamma Ray)
#KCl Concentration by Weight 		: 3.80 - 4.88 pbw (Gamma Ray)
#Mud Resistivity at BHT 		: 0.03 - 0.07 ohmm @93 degC (Resistivity)
#Fluid Density 				: 1.00 g/cc (Density)
#Neutron Tool Lithology			: Limestone (Porosity)
#Whole Mud Chlorides 			: 29883 - 35063 ppm (Porosity)
#Formation Water Salinity		: 20000 ppm Cl- (Porosity)
#Pressure and Temperature 		: from PWD and ADR (Density, Porosity)
#
#Comments:
#1) All depth are calibrated to the drillers pipe tally and are measured from drill floor.
#2) No depth correction have been made for pipe stretch or compression.
#3) LWD Resistivity Tool utilized in this run is ADR, with spacing configuration as below:
#- Deep Phase Res = 48n Spacing / 500 kHz Frequency
#- Medium Phase Res = 48in Spacing / 2Mhz Frequency
#- Shallow Phase Res = 16in Spacing / 500 kHz Frequency
#- Extra Shallow Phase Res = 16in Spacing / 2Mhz Frequency
#4) CTN Alloy type used for CTN data processing is High Nickle.
#5) Density reading might be affected by detector standoff to borehole wall while sliding.
#6) All data presented is Memory data unless otherwise stated.
#
#
